    {
      "id": "claim_f97b20344a7f46d9aeb539253f97f8a6",
      "statement": "The scheduled CI job installs openwiki globally, runs `openwiki code --update --print` with provider/model supplied via environment variables and secrets, and opens a docs pull/merge request scoped to the paths openwiki, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, and the workflow file with the commit and title \"docs: update OpenWiki\". The GitHub example runs the update step with continue-on-error, deletes transient openwiki/.run.json before the PR, and uses a trailing Propagate OpenWiki failure step (exit 1 when outcome is failure) so a partial-progress PR is still opened but the job fails on real errors.",
