    {
      "id": "claim_91bbfcd16ebf4a67a2f65e5fda3c2911",
      "statement": "The live GitHub workflow builds OpenWiki from the checked-out source (pnpm install --frozen-lockfile && pnpm build) and runs `node dist/cli/cli.js code --update` rather than the published package to dogfood unreleased changes; the published-package example workflow instead installs openwiki globally via npm. After the run it restores the protected workflow file with `git checkout -- .github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml` (guarded by if: !cancelled()) because `code --update` regenerates that file from an internal template and would otherwise drop the fork guard, deletes transient openwiki/.run.json, and opens a PR whose add-paths include openwiki, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, and the workflow file.",
